1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:02,457
The Curiosity Club.

2
00:00:02,457 --> 00:00:04,531
Episode 9.

3
00:00:04,531 --> 00:00:07,144
Eight Arms and Three Hearts.

4
00:00:07,144 --> 00:00:09,985
Here is something to listen for.

5
00:00:09,985 --> 00:00:13,693
Why was the octopus difficult to see at first?

6
00:00:13,693 --> 00:00:15,184
Ready?

7
00:00:15,184 --> 00:00:17,357
Let us find out.

8
00:00:17,357 --> 00:00:20,511
Maya and Leo visit an aquarium.

9
00:00:20,511 --> 00:00:25,085
A sign says that an octopus lives in the tank in front of them.

10
00:00:25,085 --> 00:00:29,119
They can see rocks, water, and a small crab.

11
00:00:29,119 --> 00:00:31,875
They cannot see an octopus.

12
00:00:31,875 --> 00:00:35,312
Perhaps it went shopping, Leo says.

13
00:00:35,312 --> 00:00:39,105
With eight arms, it could carry all the bags.

14
00:00:39,105 --> 00:00:42,698
The keeper points to a shape beside a rock.

15
00:00:42,698 --> 00:00:44,857
Watch closely.

16
00:00:44,857 --> 00:00:47,386
The shape slowly moves.

17
00:00:47,386 --> 00:00:51,207
A brown arm uncurls, and two eyes appear.

18
00:00:51,207 --> 00:00:54,375
The octopus has been there all along.

19
00:00:54,375 --> 00:00:58,068
Its color looked like the rocks, says Maya.

20
00:00:58,068 --> 00:01:04,545
The keeper explains that many octopuses can change their color and the appearance of their skin.

21
00:01:04,545 --> 00:01:08,096
That helps them blend into their surroundings.

22
00:01:08,096 --> 00:01:12,528
Pip tries to hide by standing beside a gray trash can.

23
00:01:12,528 --> 00:01:16,832
We can still see your flashing lights, Leo tells him.

24
00:01:16,832 --> 00:01:20,568
The octopus crawls into a sheltered space.

25
00:01:20,568 --> 00:01:23,934
The crab moves away in another direction.

26
00:01:23,934 --> 00:01:27,159
Does it have eight hearts for its eight arms?

27
00:01:27,159 --> 00:01:29,275
Maya asks.

28
00:01:29,275 --> 00:01:32,329
Three hearts, says the keeper.

29
00:01:32,329 --> 00:01:37,741
Two send blood through the gills, and one sends it around the rest of the body.

30
00:01:37,741 --> 00:01:40,752
Pip counts on his metal fingers.

31
00:01:40,752 --> 00:01:45,440
Eight arms, three hearts, and excellent hiding skills.

32
00:01:45,440 --> 00:01:47,755
Would you like eight arms?

33
00:01:47,755 --> 00:01:50,014
Leo asks Maya.

34
00:01:50,014 --> 00:01:54,730
Only until it is time to put on my jacket, she replies.

35
00:01:54,730 --> 00:01:58,806
Finding eight sleeves every morning would take forever.

36
00:01:58,806 --> 00:02:01,846
Now, a little more to discover.

37
00:02:01,846 --> 00:02:05,497
An octopus has eight arms and three hearts.

38
00:02:05,497 --> 00:02:08,607
Its gills take oxygen from water.

39
00:02:08,607 --> 00:02:13,948
Many octopuses use changes in color and skin texture as camouflage.

40
00:02:13,948 --> 00:02:22,159
These features belong to the animal's biology; the shopping trip and eight-sleeved jacket belong only to our imagination.

41
00:02:22,159 --> 00:02:25,127
Let us hear the main idea again.

42
00:02:25,127 --> 00:02:28,622
The octopus was hiding in plain sight.

43
00:02:28,622 --> 00:02:31,789
Its appearance blended with the rocks.

44
00:02:31,789 --> 00:02:37,741
At the aquarium, the children learned about its arms, hearts, and camouflage.

45
00:02:37,741 --> 00:02:42,798
Pip discovered that flashing lights are not useful when trying to hide.

46
00:02:42,798 --> 00:02:45,909
Here are three useful expressions.

47
00:02:45,909 --> 00:02:49,176
You can listen, or say them with me.

48
00:02:49,176 --> 00:02:51,562
I cannot see it yet.

49
00:02:51,562 --> 00:02:53,948
I cannot see it yet.

50
00:02:53,948 --> 00:02:56,775
Look closely beside the rock.

51
00:02:56,775 --> 00:02:59,602
Look closely beside the rock.

52
00:02:59,602 --> 00:03:02,301
How many hearts does it have?

53
00:03:02,301 --> 00:03:05,000
How many hearts does it have?

54
00:03:05,000 --> 00:03:07,713
Remember our listening question?

55
00:03:07,713 --> 00:03:11,420
Why was the octopus difficult to see at first?

56
00:03:11,420 --> 00:03:13,650
Here is the answer.

57
00:03:13,650 --> 00:03:17,187
Its appearance blended with the rocks around it.

58
00:03:17,187 --> 00:03:20,781
That kind of disguise is called camouflage.

59
00:03:20,781 --> 00:03:24,602
And here is a question just for your imagination.

60
00:03:24,602 --> 00:03:29,545
If you designed a jacket for eight arms, where would you put the pockets?

61
00:03:29,545 --> 00:03:32,798
There is more than one possible answer.

62
00:03:32,798 --> 00:03:36,193
Keep wondering, and see you next time.
